cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the archived v0.32.0 release using its version DOI below.
  The earlier v0.31.0 release is listed separately under references.
title: >-
  Geometry-consistent conservative transfer of potential-flow states
  to an embedded-boundary volume-of-fluid solver: code and numerical experiments
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Safreliy/wave_research"
abstract: >-
  Research code and numerical evidence for transferring potential-flow states
  to an embedded-boundary volume-of-fluid solver. A shared boundary trace and
  normal extension improve liquid-cell velocity reconstruction in thin flat
  surface strips. The archive includes the article PDF, manuscript source, figures, selected
  native fields, input and analysis records, independent audits, and replay
  instructions. Original code is licensed under MIT; the original manuscript,
  figures, and derived data are licensed under CC BY 4.0. Third-party material
  retains its own licence; see LICENSE.md for file-level scope.
authors:
